.vercel
node_modules/

# Written by `python -m model.refresh`. It is a local build input — the page bakes it in at
# build time, so the deployed site never reads it, and it churns on every run.
data/feed.json
# Copy of ff-jarvis data/props_model.json that build.py falls back to when the feed lacks the
# model block (the ff-jarvis checkout is shared and can sit on another branch). Same churn.
data/props_model.json
# Yahoo's own contest salary export, saved by hand before each build (no public API for this).
# Baked into the page at build time; churns every refetch.
data/dfs_yahoo.csv
